\newlabel{fig:noise_floor}{{5}{8}{The placebo null's spread (SD 0.176) compared against the window-boundary-noise floor established from stable-period DOA recomputation on 13 held-out, non-departure repositories (mean variance 11.74, SD 3.43); the true window's effect sits within 1.4 noise-floor standard deviations of zero, short of the pre-registered 2-SD bar for a genuine signal}{figure.5}{}}
